{:edb/db-before-t 2658 :edb/db-after-t 2659 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535971 50 #inst "2026-10-09T11:54:29.240Z" 13194139535971 true] [17592186192611 1020 #edb/ref 17592186377368 13194139535971 true] [17592186192611 1020 #edb/ref 17592186377375 13194139535971 true] [17592186192612 1020 #edb/ref 17592186377382 13194139535971 true] [17592186192612 1020 #edb/ref 17592186377389 13194139535971 true] [17592186192627 1020 #edb/ref 17592186377361 13194139535971 true] [17592186377361 1017 #edb/ref 17592186377362 13194139535971 true] [17592186377361 1089 "q-161596" 13194139535971 true] [17592186377361 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535971 true] [17592186377361 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072304/assets/2bb25857047d7a0200d4c58ee3756b0efa0f2d13aaca8664b1fe49414c18a461.png)\n\nConsider the set $A,$ shown above. The boundary of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n∂A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,\\,}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" 13194139535971 true] [17592186377361 1113 #uuid "28ca8dae-bb66-5179-8a04-f47a13f5a86d" 13194139535971 true] [17592186377361 1145 "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072304/assets/88f35519cf1aa01bcc9e4fb91b24c2bc2a1a823867ec2670563b0b45f2643a0a.png)\n\nFrom the diagram, the boundary points of $A$ lie on the parabola ${y}^{2}=-x.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n∂A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{y}^{2}=-x\\,}.\n$$" 13194139535971 true] [17592186377362 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377363 13194139535971 true] [17592186377362 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377364 13194139535971 true] [17592186377362 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377365 13194139535971 true] [17592186377362 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377366 13194139535971 true] [17592186377362 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377367 13194139535971 true] [17592186377362 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535971 true] [17592186377362 1041 "selection" 13194139535971 true] [17592186377362 1104 #edb/ref 17592186377366 13194139535971 true] [17592186377362 1110 #uuid "d15b0709-d032-56bd-aac5-b65c83c62380" 13194139535971 true] [17592186377363 1034 "{y}^{2}\\ge -x" 13194139535971 true] [17592186377363 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535971 true] [17592186377363 1111 #uuid "ae7e794d-b45c-5fa1-a6f8-0e6cf9bf6b06" 13194139535971 true] [17592186377364 1034 "{y}^{2}\\le -x" 13194139535971 true] [17592186377364 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535971 true] [17592186377364 1111 #uuid "1d68b7e9-6a85-5813-9310-df167cb3e035" 13194139535971 true] [17592186377365 1034 "{y}^{2}<-x" 13194139535971 true] [17592186377365 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535971 true] [17592186377365 1111 #uuid "48563982-89ee-5bb8-baec-cb82cd3e7083" 13194139535971 true] [17592186377366 1034 "{y}^{2}=-x" 13194139535971 true] [17592186377366 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535971 true] [17592186377366 1111 #uuid "9cc19fe0-3441-5697-a854-404e864c7432" 13194139535971 true] [17592186377367 1034 "{y}^{2}>-x" 13194139535971 true] [17592186377367 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535971 true] [17592186377367 1111 #uuid "161a53b4-89a7-59b6-909e-b03278987160" 13194139535971 true] [17592186377368 1017 #edb/ref 17592186377369 13194139535971 true] [17592186377368 1089 "q-161601" 13194139535971 true] [17592186377368 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535971 true] [17592186377368 1100 "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}<36}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $A$ contains none of its boundary points.\n- $A$ contains some (not all) of its boundary points.\n- $\\text{int}\\,A=A$" 13194139535971 true] [17592186377368 1113 #uuid "84f3ca08-8934-5cbf-812e-630649f3de0f" 13194139535971 true] [17592186377368 1145 "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nIn this case, the set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072304/assets/ff1f735266f66879834e02ca7601e90e40dfa7929e5796d4a3f8cb4ff2828de7.png)\n\n  \n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nNotice that, in this case, the set $A$ contains none of its boundary points. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true, while statement II is false. As we've seen, $A$ contains none of its boundary points.\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $A$ contains none of its boundary points, we must have $\\text{int}\\,A=A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" 13194139535971 true] [17592186377369 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377370 13194139535971 true] [17592186377369 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377371 13194139535971 true] [17592186377369 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377372 13194139535971 true] [17592186377369 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377373 13194139535971 true] [17592186377369 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377374 13194139535971 true] [17592186377369 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535971 true] [17592186377369 1041 "selection" 13194139535971 true] [17592186377369 1104 #edb/ref 17592186377371 13194139535971 true] [17592186377369 1110 #uuid "85322f6b-516f-5402-8c45-cb902ded5ab9" 13194139535971 true] [17592186377370 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535971 true] [17592186377370 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535971 true] [17592186377370 1111 #uuid "e172786e-070e-5772-87e4-cb0f67273db7" 13194139535971 true] [17592186377371 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535971 true] [17592186377371 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535971 true] [17592186377371 1111 #uuid "adcf6414-1d3e-5c51-825c-39866b51f27e" 13194139535971 true] [17592186377372 1034 "I only" 13194139535971 true] [17592186377372 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535971 true] [17592186377372 1111 #uuid "322b662e-5404-5635-aee4-3ab77363404f" 13194139535971 true] [17592186377373 1034 "III only" 13194139535971 true] [17592186377373 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535971 true] [17592186377373 1111 #uuid "4ed70b02-733f-5eae-8f02-c7c64dc01c85" 13194139535971 true] [17592186377374 1034 "II only" 13194139535971 true] [17592186377374 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535971 true] [17592186377374 1111 #uuid "b648d80f-658d-5211-87f3-e39e80415e4b" 13194139535971 true] [17592186377375 1017 #edb/ref 17592186377376 13194139535971 true] [17592186377375 1089 "q-161652" 13194139535971 true] [17592186377375 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535971 true] [17592186377375 1100 "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,1<{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<4}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?  \n\n- $∂A\\cap A\\ne ∅$\n- $\\text{int}\\,A\\cap ∂A=∅$\n- $A=\\text{int}\\,A$" 13194139535971 true] [17592186377375 1113 #uuid "5ee0de30-057d-5ea4-a8b3-df4f777834db" 13194139535971 true] [17592186377375 1145 "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nIn this case, the set $A$ and its boundary $∂A={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}$ are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072304/assets/2273cd843c4bfaeaff10d49d3400d7661262673639a66034638d805eef5b1e47.png)\n\n   \n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072304/assets/5e473584ef5193b434ff6c138b08c4fbd9111a37252019143b1afb2d48c913c6.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement I is false. As we've seen, $A$ contains none of its boundary points, so we must have  $∂A\\cap A=∅.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Since $\\text{int}\\,A$ contains all points in $A$ except the boundary points, we must have $\\text{int}\\,A\\cap ∂A=∅,$ where $∅$ denotes the empty set.\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $A$ contains none of its boundary points, we must have $A=\\text{int}\\,A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III  only.\"" 13194139535971 true] [17592186377376 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377377 13194139535971 true] [17592186377376 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377378 13194139535971 true] [17592186377376 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377379 13194139535971 true] [17592186377376 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377380 13194139535971 true] [17592186377376 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377381 13194139535971 true] [17592186377376 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535971 true] [17592186377376 1041 "selection" 13194139535971 true] [17592186377376 1104 #edb/ref 17592186377377 13194139535971 true] [17592186377376 1110 #uuid "c683ca29-1db4-5edb-92a8-944119592610" 13194139535971 true] [17592186377377 1034 "II and III  only" 13194139535971 true] [17592186377377 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535971 true] [17592186377377 1111 #uuid "a3d796fa-a51e-50a8-8acc-fedc48733837" 13194139535971 true] [17592186377378 1034 "I  only" 13194139535971 true] [17592186377378 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535971 true] [17592186377378 1111 #uuid "281888a4-8299-5625-95f0-9f5d0f785306" 13194139535971 true] [17592186377379 1034 "I and III  only" 13194139535971 true] [17592186377379 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535971 true] [17592186377379 1111 #uuid "98dfc48c-f4a7-54d5-bd49-55b4cbac5dc7" 13194139535971 true] [17592186377380 1034 "III  only" 13194139535971 true] [17592186377380 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535971 true] [17592186377380 1111 #uuid "b878bb07-2cb0-5f66-a06f-838dc9fcfcce" 13194139535971 true] [17592186377381 1034 "II  only" 13194139535971 true] [17592186377381 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454