029-99b9-a7becab58e6c" 13194139535971 true] [17592186377389 1145 "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072304/assets/f4ee8fbf9a7670a7d0e0b7488bccbf014f8db8fff0154c7db025f2b071aec566.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072304/assets/9fc733f6966b016c93b6ee6a305c5af5ee4fa432dad5d95e28061fd2a0d33efb.png)\n\nSo, in this case, the interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0<{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<4,\\,0<y<2}.\n$$" 13194139535971 true] [17592186377390 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377391 13194139535971 true] [17592186377390 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377392 13194139535971 true] [17592186377390 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377393 13194139535971 true] [17592186377390 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377394 13194139535971 true] [17592186377390 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377395 13194139535971 true] [17592186377390 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535971 true] [17592186377390 1041 "selection" 13194139535971 true] [17592186377390 1104 #edb/ref 17592186377392 13194139535971 true] [17592186377390 1110 #uuid "4917a447-5696-5f04-92f9-a8495961982b" 13194139535971 true] [17592186377391 1034 "0\\le {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 4" 13194139535971 true] [17592186377391 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535971 true] [17592186377391 1111 #uuid "802abbf3-238f-50ff-9139-83436dcf5148" 13194139535971 true] [17592186377392 1034 "0<{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<4" 13194139535971 true] [17592186377392 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535971 true] [17592186377392 1111 #uuid "75b915bb-2128-5d